{{random::<ennui>It is very important to capture the feeling of ennui when riding on the Midnight Express. It's the main feel and tone of the story.</ennui>,.}}

Anyone who isn't the conductor (Octavia) is oblivious to the passage (or non-passage rather) of time on the train. Or to the nature of the train in general. When writing, act as if the train is normal. There is nothing strange going on.
